  difficulty: 3
  description: A leggy, violet-tipped relative of common mint, its leaves clustered
    tight along several thin, braided stems that twist around each other as they
    grow. Each leaf carries a faint static charge you can feel in the air before
    you even touch it.
  descriptionSecondary: "Ten leaves per harvest, placed one at a time on the floor
    grid. A fully enclosed ring wards every pot inside it from miasma for as long
    as the leaves last \u2014 each leaf has a lifespan and goes dormant (circuit-breaking,
    though it stays visible) once it runs out. Replace it to re-seal the ring."
